From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: range and selection Paste, CanPaste, GetPoint; SetText at an offset (2053)

riched20: ITextRange / ITextSelection Paste, CanPaste, GetPoint, ScrollIntoView; SetText at an offset.

Paste puts the text of the clipboard (or of a data object given in the
variant) in the range, CanPaste says whether there is such text for the
format (0, CF_UNICODETEXT or CF_TEXT), GetPoint gives the start or end of a
range as a point in the window or on the screen, and the selection answers
all of them and ScrollIntoView. ITextRange::SetText no longer replaces the
text between the start of the text and the range when the caret is not at
the start (the insert took the selection's two cursors as a selection), and
the range it leaves ends where the new text does.
---
--- a/dlls/riched20/richole.c
+++ b/dlls/riched20/richole.c
@@ -1593,7 +1593,7 @@
 {
     ITextRangeImpl *This = impl_from_ITextRange(me);
     ME_TextEditor *editor;
-    ME_Cursor cursor;
+    ME_Cursor cursor, saved[2];
     ME_Style *style;
     int len;
 
@@ -1620,17 +1620,23 @@
 
